DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260413
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260414
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: Nineteen tribunals
DESCRIPTION:Nineteen appellate tribunals were at work. Appeals decided by 2
 1 and 27 April were to take effect through a supplementary roll before pol
 ling\, and a pending appeal gave no right to vote. Source: https://api.sci
 .gov.in/supremecourt/2025/64235/64235_2025_1_53_70166_Order_13-Apr-2026.pd
 f More: https://offtheroll.in/india/process/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/process/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sc-2026-05-27@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260527
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260528
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: The Supreme Court upholds the revision
DESCRIPTION:The Court disposed of the petitions. It held that the revision 
 has its legal basis in section 21(3) of the Representation of the People A
 ct read with Article 324\, that it was proportionate\, and that its docume
 nt list\, with Aadhaar added\, was not arbitrary. The Commission may enqui
 re into citizenship only for electoral purposes and must refer doubtful ca
 ses to the competent authority of the Central Government. People domiciled
  in Bihar whose names were wrongly deleted as absent\, dead\, shifted or d
 uplicate may seek judicial review. Source: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremec
 ourt/2025/35785/35785_2025_1_1501_71617_Judgement_27-May-2026.pdf More: ht
 tps://offtheroll.in/india/process/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/process/
END:VEVENT
