UID:court-list-01@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: A petition against deletions in Maharashtra's revisi
 on\, W.P.(C) No. 1330 of 2026. The Court issued notice to the Election Com
 mission on 26 October
DESCRIPTION:A petition against deletions in Maharashtra's revision\, W.P.(C
 ) No. 1330 of 2026. The Court issued notice to the Election Commission on 
 26 October. The petition is listed for hearing. On 26 October the Court de
 clined to extend the time for claims and objections or to stop the final r
 oll before hearing the Commission. Court: Supreme Court. Source: LawChakra
 \, https://lawchakra.in/supreme-court/maharashtra-sir-notice-eci/ More: ht
 tps://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-51
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-46@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:BJP march and public meeting on the SIR in Malappuram
DESCRIPTION:A BJP march in Malappuram followed by a public meeting\, which 
 the party says is part of its nationwide campaign to explain the need for 
 the revision. Organised by Bharatiya Janata Party\, Malappuram (State vice
 -president V. Unnikrishnan inaugurated the planning meeting) (a political 
 party). Place: Malappuram (route and venue not stated). Source: https://ww
 w.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/bjp-to-hold-sir-march-on-november-6/ar
 ticle71623341.ece
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-67@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:'Jantar Mantar at Kochi' march and meeting against the SIR
DESCRIPTION:The actor Prakash Raj led a march from Marine Drive to a meetin
 g at Rajendra Maidan\, where the group's founder\, Abhijeet Dipke\, spoke.
  The protest called for the revision to be withdrawn and the Chief Electio
 n Commissioner to resign. The organisers put the march at about 500\, and 
 the state president of the DYFI\, Chintha Jerome\, took part. Organised by
  Cockroach Janta Party. Place: From Marine Drive to Rajendra Maidan\, Koch
 i. Source: https://www.freepressjournal.in/india/cockroach-janta-party-fou
 nder-abhijeet-dipke-attacks-pm-modi-at-kochi-rally-questions-electoral-rol
 l-revision
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-03@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Supreme Court (listed tentatively): The petitions alleging that dec
 isions of the Election Commission\, those on the revision among them\, wer
 e taken without the agreement of the two Election Commissioners\, led by W
 .P.(C) No. 1246 of 2026
DESCRIPTION:The petitions alleging that decisions of the Election Commissio
 n\, those on the revision among them\, were taken without the agreement of
  the two Election Commissioners\, led by W.P.(C) No. 1246 of 2026. On 27 O
 ctober the petitioners were given 10 days to file a rejoinder to the Commi
 ssion's counter affidavit. The bench listed the matter for this date tenta
 tively. The court listed the matter for this date tentatively. Court: Supr
 eme Court. Source: LiveLaw\, https://www.livelaw.in/top-stories/supreme-co
 urt-election-commission-functioning-cec-gyanesh-kumar-556132 More: https:/
 /offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-53
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
