DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: The petition of two transparency activists on Delhi'
 s revision\, W.P.(C) No. 1188 of 2026\, and an application they were told 
 to file on the Commission's letter about Form 6
DESCRIPTION:The petition of two transparency activists on Delhi's revision\
 , W.P.(C) No. 1188 of 2026\, and an application they were told to file on 
 the Commission's letter about Form 6. The matter is listed for hearing. On
  4 November the Court declined to pass urgent orders and asked the petitio
 ners to file their application before this date. Court: Supreme Court. Sou
 rce: Hindustan Times\, https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/sir-don-t
 -fear-supreme-court-tells-delhi-voters-struck-off-draft-electoral-roll-101
 793776921886.html More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-61
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-07@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: A petition by a group of advocates for guidelines on
  processions and protests near the Supreme Court\, after the Opposition's 
 march of 12 October against the Chief Election Commissioner
DESCRIPTION:A petition by a group of advocates for guidelines on procession
 s and protests near the Supreme Court\, after the Opposition's march of 12
  October against the Chief Election Commissioner. On 3 November the Court 
 sought replies from Mallikarjun Kharge\, Rahul Gandhi and the Centre\, and
  the Centre said it would reply by this date. Court: Supreme Court. Source
 : Hindustan Times\, https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/supreme-cour
 t-rahul-gandhi-mallikarjun-kharge-india-bloc-protest-gyanesh-kumar-1017937
 02344380.html More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-62
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-29@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Delhi Chalo marches and Constitution Day event
DESCRIPTION:The Congress announced six Delhi Chalo marches from Rajasthan\,
  Haryana and Uttar Pradesh on 25 November\, ending in an event in Delhi on
  Constitution Day\, 26 November\, as the last stage of its 'Vote bachao\, 
 Desh bachao' campaign. Organised by Indian National Congress (state units)
  (a political party). Place: Six marches from Rajasthan\, Haryana and Utta
 r Pradesh to Delhi. Source: https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/congres
 s-campaign-against-vote-chori-to-help-re-enroll-voters-whose-names-were-de
 leted-in-sir/article71548466.ece
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev-69@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Rally on Anna Salai\, Chennai\, against the SIR
DESCRIPTION:A rally that the collective announced at a press conference at 
 the Chennai Press Club on 10 November\, as part of what it called a nation
 wide day of action against the revision. The political economist Parakala 
 Prabhakar\, the Carnatic vocalist T.M. Krishna\, Thomas Franco\, a former 
 General Secretary of the All India Bank Officers' Confederation\, and the 
 collective's co-convenor Radhika Ganesh spoke at the press conference. The
  collective demanded an inquiry into the fall in Tamil Nadu's roll\, which
  it put at 74.07 lakh names. Prabhakar called for the revision to be scrap
 ped and for every eligible voter whose name was deleted to be restored. Or
 ganised by Independent Young Citizens Collective\, part of People Against 
 SIR. Place: Anna Salai\, Chennai. Source: https://www.thehindu.com/news/na
 tional/tamil-nadu/over-74-lakh-voters-missing-from-tamil-nadu-electoral-ro
 lls-says-citizens-collective/article71685695.ece
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/events/
END:VEVENT
