UID:court-list-05@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Bombay High Court: Petitions against the exclusion of electors in M
 aharashtra's revision
DESCRIPTION:Petitions against the exclusion of electors in Maharashtra's re
 vision. The Election Commission asked for them to be deferred because the 
 Supreme Court is hearing the revision. The petitions are listed for hearin
 g. The High Court has given no view on their merits. Court: Bombay High Co
 urt. Source: LawChakra\, https://lawchakra.in/high-court/bombay-high-court
 /maharashtra-sir-bombay-hc/ More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-
 court-34
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-09@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Court of the First Additional Sessions Judge: A revision petition b
 y the Banbhoolpura police against a Haldwani magistrate's order of 6 Octob
 er to register an FIR over Form 7s filed to delete 28 electors in the name
  of a booth level agent who says he did not file them
DESCRIPTION:A revision petition by the Banbhoolpura police against a Haldwa
 ni magistrate's order of 6 October to register an FIR over Form 7s filed t
 o delete 28 electors in the name of a booth level agent who says he did no
 t file them. On 30 October the court refused to stay the order. The revisi
 on petition is listed for hearing. Court: Court of the First Additional Se
 ssions Judge. Source: Dainik Jagran\, https://www.jagran.com/uttarakhand/n
 ainital-haldwani-court-rejects-police-plea-in-28-voter-deletion-case-40433
 301.html More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-69
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-08@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: Petitions by the RJD Member of Parliament Manoj Jha 
 and an advocate challenging section 16 of the Act of 2023 on the Chief Ele
 ction Commissioner and the Election Commissioners\, which bars civil and c
 riminal proceedings against them for their official acts
DESCRIPTION:Petitions by the RJD Member of Parliament Manoj Jha and an advo
 cate challenging section 16 of the Act of 2023 on the Chief Election Commi
 ssioner and the Election Commissioners\, which bars civil and criminal pro
 ceedings against them for their official acts. The Court issued notice to 
 the Centre and the Election Commission on 4 November. The petitions are li
 sted for hearing. Court: Supreme Court. Source: The Hindu\, https://www.th
 ehindu.com/news/national/sc-seeks-centre-ec-response-on-law-giving-blanket
 -lifelong-immunity-to-cec-election-commissioners/article71664699.ece More:
  https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-64
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
